<title>GERMANY: German Benckiser plans to float units on bourse.</title>
<headline>German Benckiser plans to float units on bourse.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAFEN, Germany 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German cosmetics and chemicals group Joh. A. Benckiser GmbH plans to split its operations into two separate units and list both groups on the bourse this year, chief executive Peter Harf told a German newspaper.</p>
<p>Daily Handelsblatt said Benckiser plans to list its cosmetics activities on the New York bourse this spring and the rest of its activities, including cleansers, on the Amsterdam bourse before the end of the year.</p>
<p>The group also raised its 1996 group sales to 5.3 billion marks ($3.2 billion) from 4.8 billion marks, the paper reported.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.636 German Marks)</p>
